   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 374 of the laws of 2014 amending the education law\nrelating to the leasing of real property by boards of cooperative educational\nservices, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8674",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8674-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4, Chap 374 of 2014",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8674\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 374 of the laws of 2014 amending the education\nlaw relating to the leasing of real property by boards of cooperative\neducational services, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo extend authorization for BOCES to lease with private entities for 20\nyears till July 1, 2029.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends 374 of the laws of 2014 amending the education law to\nextend the effective date to July 1, 2029.\n\nSection 2 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPrior to 2014, Boards of Cooperative Educational Services (BOCES) could\nonly enter into leases with a maximum duration of ten years.  Chapter\n374 of the laws of 2014 gave BOCES authorization to enter into 20-year\nleases with private entities. Longer leases have allowed BOCES to better\nplan future projects, save costs, and provide greater efficiencies to\nthe overall operations of their districts.\n\nThis authorization is scheduled to expire on July 1, 2024. This bill\nwould extend for a further 5 years, until July 1, 2029.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
